From: =?UTF-8?q?K=C3=A9vin=20R=C3=A9mondi=C3=A8re?= <kevin@localhost>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:30:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/54] vulkan: fuse hc_combine chain into one kernel
 ([TAG_HC_COMBINE_FUSED] S2, soup)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fuses the per-layer hyper-connection combine of qwen4exp (96x per decode
token): SIGMOID -> SCALE(2.0) -> SCALE(2.0) -> [RESHAPE w] and RESHAPE(b)
-> REPEAT_4D -> MUL(b,w) -> ADD(res, mul) become ONE kernel
  dst = res + b * ((sig*2.0)*2.0)
while the SIGMOID stays a normal unary kernel node (recomputing
1/(1+exp(-x)) in a different shader broke byte-exactness vs unary.comp
codegen — validated by full-model checksum A/B).

- matcher by DEPENDENCIES (lesson S1: never assume DFS node order);
  requires uses==1 intermediates, exact 2.0f scale factors, f32,
  contiguous i rows, 4 scalars/thread direct (i,j,k) indexing
  (no flat idx / fastdiv / fastmod — GPT-5.6 review), local_size 64,
  grid (n_embd/4/64, hc, nt)
- precise on every intermediate: mul-then-add as two rounded steps,
  no FMA contraction
- skip-set mechanism (GDN_ZC pattern) elides SCALE/SCALE/REPEAT/MUL
- sync: direct reads of block_out and sig registered in the
  overlaps_unsynced checks
- gate env GGML_VK_DISABLE_HC_COMBINE_FUSED; disabled under
  GGML_VULKAN_CHECK_RESULTS

Validated on the 125B (FOLD.v2): byte-exact (probe/France/probs/texts
checksums match the pre-change reference), 96/96 chains fused,
~1% GPU time saved (368ms GPU on a 29.4s-GPU session), +0.74% wall-clock
on the A/B (4+4 runs).
